---
import '../../public/css/v4.css';
import '../../public/css/agents.css';
import '../../public/css/technical-foundation.css';
import '../../public/css/technical-foundation-next.css';
import '../../public/css/marketing-shell.css';
import BrandHead from '../components/BrandHead.astro';
import MarketingFooter from '../components/marketing/MarketingFooter.astro';
import MarketingHeader from '../components/marketing/MarketingHeader.astro';
import ExplainedTerm from '../components/marketing/ExplainedTerm.astro';
import 'boxicons/css/boxicons.min.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <BrandHead
        title="How Fluxzero keeps your product running — Fluxzero"
        description="See how Fluxzero gives every product the correctness, security, privacy, recovery, auditability, and scale enterprises require from day zero."
    />
</head>
<body class="v4-page agent4-page cloud-proof-page cloud-proof-next-page">
    <MarketingHeader active="how-it-works" />

    <main>
        <header class="cloud-proof-hero cloud-proof-next-hero">
            <span class="cloud-proof-hero__sun" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <p class="cloud-proof-hero__back" data-reveal><a href="/how-it-works#layers-title" data-browser-back><i class="bx bx-left-arrow-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i> Back</a></p>
                <p class="cloud-proof-next__eyebrow" data-reveal>Technical foundation</p>
                <h1 data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">How Fluxzero keeps<br><span>your product running.</span></h1>
                <p class="cloud-proof-hero__lead" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">Enterprises expect critical systems to keep their promises under pressure. That standard matters long before a product reaches enterprise size. With Fluxzero, it is built into every product from day zero.</p>
            </div>
        </header>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="customer-isolation" aria-labelledby="customer-isolation-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">01 · Foundation by default</p>
                    <h2 id="customer-isolation-title">Every cluster comes with<br><span>the full Fluxzero foundation.</span></h2>
                    <p>A cluster is a dedicated environment containing a product’s applications, data, and technical foundation. Every cluster is isolated from every other cluster, and its applications stay off the public internet.</p>
                    <p>From the first deployment, its foundation provides correctness, security, privacy, recovery, auditability, and controlled scale. These guarantees are built into every cluster—not added later by the product team.</p>
                </header>

                <figure class="cloud-diagram model-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="Applications run inside a dedicated product cluster with the complete Fluxzero foundation">
                    <div class="model-diagram__external"><i class="bx bx-globe" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>External traffic</strong><span aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
                    <div class="model-diagram__frame">
                        <span class="model-diagram__cluster-label"><i class="bx bx-shield-quarter" aria-hidden="true"></i>Your product cluster</span>
                        <div class="model-diagram__applications">
                            <div class="model-diagram__application model-diagram__application--three" aria-label="Application A, three running tasks">
                                <span class="model-diagram__instance model-diagram__instance--back" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                <span class="model-diagram__instance model-diagram__instance--middle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                <div class="model-diagram__instance model-diagram__instance--front">
                                    <span><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Application A</strong><small>3 tasks</small></span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="model-diagram__application model-diagram__application--two" aria-label="Application B, two running tasks">
                                <span class="model-diagram__instance model-diagram__instance--back" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                <div class="model-diagram__instance model-diagram__instance--front">
                                    <span><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Application B</strong><small>2 tasks</small></span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="model-diagram__connections" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
                        <div class="model-diagram__cloud">
                            <span class="logo-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <strong>Fluxzero foundation</strong>
                            <div class="model-diagram__capabilities">
                                <span>Correctness</span>
                                <span>Security</span>
                                <span>Privacy</span>
                                <span>Recovery</span>
                                <span>Auditability</span>
                                <span>Scale</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <figcaption class="sr-only">Every cluster isolates one product and includes the complete Fluxzero foundation from its first deployment.</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="valid-state" aria-labelledby="valid-state-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">02 · Correctness</p>
                    <h2 id="valid-state-title">Every action leaves the product<br><span>in a valid state.</span></h2>
                    <p>Your product defines what must always be true. Fluxzero makes sure those rules still hold when many users act at the same time. A change either succeeds completely or leaves nothing half-finished behind.</p>
                </header>
                <figure class="cloud-diagram ticket-sequence" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="Buyer A reserves ticket 42 first. Buyer B then attempts to reserve it and is rejected.">
                    <ol>
                        <li class="ticket-sequence__accepted">
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__number">1</span>
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__buyer"><i class="bx bx-user" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Buyer A</strong></span>
                            <i class="bx bx-right-arrow-alt ticket-sequence__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__ticket"><i class="bx bx-purchase-tag-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Ticket 42</strong><small>Available</small></span>
                            <i class="bx bx-right-arrow-alt ticket-sequence__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__outcome"><i class="bx bx-check" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Reserved</strong></span>
                        </li>
                        <li class="ticket-sequence__rejected">
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__number">2</span>
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__buyer"><i class="bx bx-user" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Buyer B</strong></span>
                            <i class="bx bx-right-arrow-alt ticket-sequence__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__ticket"><i class="bx bx-purchase-tag-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Ticket 42</strong><small>Already reserved</small></span>
                            <i class="bx bx-right-arrow-alt ticket-sequence__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span class="ticket-sequence__outcome"><i class="bx bx-x" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Rejected</strong></span>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                    <figcaption class="sr-only">Buyer A acts first and reserves ticket 42. Buyer B acts second and cannot reserve the same ticket.</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="recoverable-work" aria-labelledby="recoverable-work-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">03 · Reliability and recovery</p>
                    <h2 id="recoverable-work-title">Failure does not mean<br><span>lost work.</span></h2>
                    <p>Fluxzero records work before your application starts it. If an instance restarts, the work waits and continues when it is ready. One failing part does not stop the rest of the product.</p>
                    <p>Fix the cause, then replay only the affected work. Failed work remains visible and recoverable without first building a separate recovery system.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="cloud-proof-next__diagram-stack cloud-proof-next__diagram-stack--split">
                    <figure class="cloud-diagram request-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="A request is recorded before it is handled">
                        <div class="request-diagram__step"><i class="bx bx-log-in" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Received</span></div>
                        <div class="request-diagram__track" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
                        <div class="request-diagram__step request-diagram__step--record"><i class="bx bx-layer" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Recorded</span></div>
                        <div class="request-diagram__track" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
                        <div class="request-diagram__step"><i class="bx bx-check" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Handled</span></div>
                        <figcaption>Recorded first. Handled when the application is ready.</figcaption>
                    </figure>
                    <figure class="cloud-diagram replay-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2" aria-label="A failed message is fixed and replayed over a selected part of the recorded timeline">
                        <div class="replay-diagram__timeline" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
                        <ol>
                            <li><span>1</span></li>
                            <li><span>2</span></li>
                            <li class="is-failed"><i class="bx bx-x" aria-hidden="true"></i><small>Failed</small></li>
                            <li><span>4</span></li>
                            <li><span>5</span></li>
                        </ol>
                        <div class="replay-diagram__fix"><i class="bx bx-wrench" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Fix</span></div>
                        <div class="replay-diagram__return"><i class="bx bx-revision" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Replay</span></div>
                        <figcaption>Repair the cause. Replay the affected range.</figcaption>
                    </figure>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">04 · Privacy and data control</p>
                    <h2 id="privacy-title">Keep the history.<br><span>Remove the personal data.</span></h2>
                    <p>Sensitive values stay separate from the durable history. Trusted code can use them without exposing them in logs, and they can be permanently erased without destroying the surrounding record.</p>
                    <p>Fluxzero protects <ExplainedTerm id="pii-definition" label="PII data" definition="Personally identifiable information: data that can identify a person directly or indirectly, such as an email address." /> and makes it erasable while you decide how it is used. Each recipient sees only the data the product allows. These controls make data minimization and erasure practical and support requirements under <ExplainedTerm id="gdpr-definition" label="GDPR" definition="The European Union’s General Data Protection Regulation, governing how organizations collect, use, and protect personal data." /> in Europe and California’s <ExplainedTerm id="ccpa-definition" label="CCPA" definition="The California Consumer Privacy Act, amended by the CPRA, including rights to access, delete, and limit the use of personal information." />.</p>
                </header>
                <figure class="cloud-diagram privacy-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="A protected email value is removed while the non-sensitive order history remains">
                    <div class="privacy-diagram__record privacy-diagram__record--before">
                        <strong>Order 42</strong>
                        <span>size&nbsp; M</span>
                        <span class="is-protected"><i class="bx bx-lock-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i> email</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="privacy-diagram__action"><i class="bx bx-trash" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Delete personal data</span></div>
                    <div class="privacy-diagram__record privacy-diagram__record--after">
                        <strong>Order 42</strong>
                        <span>size&nbsp; M</span>
                        <span class="is-redacted"><i class="bx bx-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> redacted</span>
                    </div>
                    <figcaption class="sr-only">The protected email is erased while the rest of order 42 remains available.</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section cloud-proof-model" id="protected" aria-labelledby="protected-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">05 · Secure by design</p>
                    <h2 id="protected-title">Your applications stay off<br> <span>the public internet.</span></h2>
                    <p>Fluxzero receives public web traffic at its managed edge. Your applications pull incoming traffic and send outbound traffic over connections they open themselves, so none of them needs a public endpoint.</p>
                    <p>Your applications still decide who someone is, what they may do, and whether a request is valid. Fluxzero gives every request a protected path to those product decisions.</p>
                </header>

                <figure class="cloud-diagram secure-edge-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="Public traffic enters the Fluxzero foundation while applications pull and send traffic over outbound connections and expose no public endpoints">
                    <div class="secure-edge-diagram__internet">
                        <i class="bx bx-globe" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <strong>Public internet</strong>
                    </div>
                    <div class="secure-edge-diagram__public-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                    <div class="secure-edge-diagram__foundation">
                        <i class="bx bx-shield-quarter" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <strong>Fluxzero foundation</strong>
                        <small>Traffic in and out</small>
                    </div>
                    <div class="secure-edge-diagram__connection">
                        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <strong><i class="bx bx-lock-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i>Applications pull and send</strong>
                        <small>Outbound connections</small>
                    </div>
                    <div class="secure-edge-diagram__cluster">
                        <span><i class="bx bx-shield" aria-hidden="true"></i>Your cluster</span>
                        <div><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Application A</strong><small>No public endpoint</small></div>
                        <div><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Application B</strong><small>No public endpoint</small></div>
                    </div>
                    <figcaption class="sr-only">Fluxzero receives public traffic while applications stay private and pull and send traffic over connections they open themselves.</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section cloud-proof-next-audit" id="audit-trail" aria-labelledby="audit-trail-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">06 · Auditability</p>
                    <h2 id="audit-trail-title">If it is not in the audit trail,<br><span>it did not happen.</span></h2>
                    <p>Fluxzero records every request and response, together with every internal message and interaction that followed. Their connection is preserved from the first cause to the final outcome.</p>
                    <p>The dashboard makes that history searchable from beginning to end. It shows what happened, where progress stopped, and which part of the product was affected. This complete operational view is available without setup. <a href="/monitoring">Explore the monitoring dashboard.</a></p>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__statement">Current state tells you what is true. The audit trail tells you why—and everything that happened along the way.</p>
                </header>
                <figure class="cloud-proof-next__audit-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="An example ticket reservation audit trail is available in the Fluxzero dashboard">
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__audit-stream">
                        <strong>Ticket reservation · #42</strong>
                        <ol>
                            <li><time>09:41:02.103</time><span><small>Request</small>Reserve ticket</span></li>
                            <li><time>09:41:02.114</time><span><small>Event</small>Ticket reserved</span></li>
                            <li><time>09:41:02.119</time><span><small>Response</small>Reservation confirmed</span></li>
                        </ol>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__audit-line" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__dashboard">
                        <div class="cloud-proof-next__dashboard-header"><span class="logo-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Fluxzero dashboard</strong><small>Available without setup</small></div>
                        <div class="cloud-proof-next__dashboard-grid">
                            <span><i class="bx bx-list-ul" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Audit trail</strong><small>Every interaction</small></span>
                            <span><i class="bx bx-git-branch" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Traces</strong><small>Cause to outcome</small></span>
                            <span><i class="bx bx-error" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Issues</strong><small>Occurrences and versions</small></span>
                            <span><i class="bx bx-line-chart" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Application graph</strong><small>Flow and performance</small></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <figcaption class="sr-only">A ticket reservation can be followed through each connected message in the Fluxzero dashboard.</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="bounded-traffic" aria-labelledby="bounded-traffic-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">07 · Bounded traffic</p>
                    <h2 id="bounded-traffic-title">Traffic spikes don’t overwhelm<br> <span>your applications.</span></h2>
                    <p>Fluxzero limits how much work reaches each application at once. Excess demand waits outside instead of flooding it, so DDoS-like overload cannot cascade through the product.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="cloud-proof-next__diagram-stack cloud-proof-next__scale-stack">
                    <figure class="cloud-diagram capacity-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="Incoming work passes through a bounded capacity gate">
                        <div class="capacity-diagram__incoming" aria-hidden="true">
                            <span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="capacity-diagram__gate">
                            <strong>Bounded capacity</strong>
                            <div><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="is-empty"></span><span class="is-empty"></span></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="capacity-diagram__application"><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Application</span></div>
                        <div class="capacity-diagram__held"><i class="bx bx-pause" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Held back</span></div>
                        <figcaption>Excess demand stays outside the application.</figcaption>
                    </figure>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="independent-scale" aria-labelledby="independent-scale-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">08 · Independent scale</p>
                    <h2 id="independent-scale-title">Each part of the product<br> <span>scales independently.</span></h2>
                    <p>Slow work cannot stall the rest of the product. Capacity grows exactly where it is needed.</p>
                    <p>Start as one application, then split it into separate services—or bring it together again—without changing what the product does.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="cloud-proof-next__diagram-stack cloud-proof-next__scale-stack">
                    <figure class="cloud-diagram lanes-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="Ticketing, payments, and notifications keep their own progress and capacity">
                        <div class="lanes-diagram__source"><i class="bx bx-layer" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Recorded events</span></div>
                        <div class="lanes-diagram__lane"><strong>Ticketing</strong><span class="lane-progress lane-progress--full"></span><i class="bx bx-check" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <div class="lanes-diagram__lane lanes-diagram__lane--paused"><strong>Payments</strong><span class="lane-progress lane-progress--short"></span><i class="bx bx-pause" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <div class="lanes-diagram__lane"><strong>Notifications</strong><span class="lane-progress lane-progress--full"></span><i class="bx bx-check" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
                        <figcaption>Independent progress keeps slow work isolated.</figcaption>
                    </figure>
                </div>
                <div class="cloud-proof-next__shape" data-reveal>
                    <div><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>One application</strong></div>
                    <span><i class="bx bx-transfer-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><small>same product behavior</small></span>
                    <div><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><i class="bx bx-cube-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Independent services</strong></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="evolution" aria-labelledby="evolution-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">09 · Safe evolution</p>
                    <h2 id="evolution-title">New capabilities can reach<br><span>into the product’s past.</span></h2>
                    <p>Your product can change without abandoning the data and decisions it has already recorded. Older information remains usable by the current application, even as the product evolves.</p>
                    <p>Add a new capability later and run it across existing history. It can work retroactively instead of starting empty on the day it is introduced.</p>
                </header>
                <figure class="cloud-proof-next__evolution-diagram" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="A long audit trail feeds existing product capabilities and customer rewards added later">
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__history-heading">
                        <span><i class="bx bx-history" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Audit trail</strong></span>
                        <small>The complete product history</small>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__history">
                        <span class="cloud-proof-next__history-ellipsis" aria-hidden="true">…</span>
                        <div><small>Event</small><strong>Ticket reserved</strong></div>
                        <div><small>Event</small><strong>Payment received</strong></div>
                        <div><small>Event</small><strong>Reservation confirmed</strong></div>
                        <span class="cloud-proof-next__history-ellipsis" aria-hidden="true">…</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__evolution-path"><span>Every capability can use the full history</span></div>
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__capabilities">
                        <div class="cloud-proof-next__existing-capabilities">
                            <small>Already running</small>
                            <div>
                                <span><i class="bx bx-calendar-check" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Ticket reservations</strong></span>
                                <span><i class="bx bx-credit-card" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Payment processing</strong></span>
                                <span><i class="bx bx-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Customer confirmations</strong></span>
                                <span><i class="bx bx-x-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Cancellation handling</strong></span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="cloud-proof-next__retroactive">
                            <small>Added later</small>
                            <span><i class="bx bx-gift" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Customer rewards</strong><em>Built from all previous purchases</em></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <figcaption class="sr-only">Ticket reservations, payment processing, customer confirmations, cancellation handling, and customer rewards can all use the complete product history.</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="cloud-proof-section cloud-proof-next-section" id="zero-ops" aria-labelledby="zero-ops-title">
            <div class="v4-shell cloud-proof-shell">
                <header class="cloud-proof-copy" data-reveal>
                    <p class="cloud-proof-next__number">10 · ZeroOps cloud</p>
                    <h2 id="zero-ops-title">Launch with production-grade<br> <span>operations already in place.</span></h2>
                    <p>Deploy to as many clusters as your products require. Fluxzero operates every one from its first deployment, with point-in-time recovery backed by automated backups and a complete monitoring view available as soon as it starts.</p>
                    <p>Create a new cluster or duplicate one from an earlier point in time. Each cluster can be paused without losing its identity or state, while access and secrets remain protected.</p>
                </header>
                <figure class="cloud-proof-next__operations" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" aria-label="Production and acceptance clusters include operated lifecycle controls, point-in-time recovery backed by automated backups, and monitoring">
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__operations-clusters" aria-label="Production and acceptance clusters">
                        <div><i class="bx bx-network-chart" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Production</strong><small>Cluster</small></div>
                        <div><i class="bx bx-network-chart" aria-hidden="true"></i><strong>Acceptance</strong><small>Cluster</small></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cloud-proof-next__operations-columns">
                        <div class="cloud-proof-next__operations-lifecycle">
                            <strong>Built into every cluster</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li><i class="bx bx-rocket" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><strong>Deploy</strong><small>Start a new cluster</small></span></li>
                                <li><i class="bx bx-pause-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><strong>Pause and resume</strong><small>Preserve identity and state</small></span></li>
                                <li><i class="bx bx-revision" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><strong>Point-in-time recovery</strong><small>Automated backups; restore or duplicate</small></span></li>
                                <li><i class="bx bx-key" aria-hidden="true"></i><span><strong>Protected access</strong><small>Secrets stay encrypted</small></span></li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="cloud-proof-next__operations-lifecycle">
                            <strong>Monitoring in every cluster</strong>
                            <ul>
